Package: ezrintelligence
Type: Package
Title: Single-Line Language-Model Summaries for Analysis Tables
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Andreas", "Schellewald", email = "aschellewald@acm.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Turns a finished analysis table into written findings with one
    call to a large language model. Provides a registry of named prompt
    templates written to an analyst standard (quote only figures present in
    the data, treat differences inside the margin of error as noise, name the
    base), a context object carrying sample size, question wording and
    precision alongside the table, helpers that summarise one table or a whole
    named list of report sections, and slide title and bullet drafting for
    presentation decks. API keys are read from the operating system credential
    store or the conventional environment variable, so secrets never appear in
    scripts. Model access is through the 'ellmer' package, which supports
    commercial providers and locally served open-weight models alike.
